{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Eczj7bPzkjnaAZjzTdLQZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-13 23:00 +07\n2\t# Task: slice 7c, the composition and the compose and fencing rows (codex implements)\n3\t\n4\tWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c`, branch `srvm-phase7c`, from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (= master + 7a custody on rows + 7b holder export/recovery v2/driver lower/install checks). 7a-7d land on `srvm-phase7`; master only when 7d is green, so suites 7c/7d own are red until you re-base them. Your work will be reviewed by a NON-codex reviewer (Fable) with mutants: make every mutant below catchable by a test. Read first: `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`; `collab/phase7-plan.md` (3.4 crash cuts, 3.5 publication of successors, 3.6 authority vs sealed refs, 3.8, 3.9, section 4 slice 7c is your scope); `collab/7a-report.md`; `collab/1792450000000-engineer-7b-holder-export.report.md` (what exists now: export prepare/encode, recovery v2, rehydrate-fenced, the driver, `source-index` as a required composition seam); `collab/7b-review.md` (Fable's findings F1-F3: F1 and F2 are test additions YOU land first as the slice's first commit-sized step, F3 is your re-base); `docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` 7.7, 7.11; `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` (as amended); `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{compose,rows,holder/*,authority/*,custody,ledger}.cljc`. Owner rulings: fork custody nil; the REPL custody gap is accepted until phase 8 (you do NOT touch `yin.repl/main.cljc`: the plain-composition test is re-based on a semantic-register receiver and the REPL's `:custody` branch is only documented inert, report it); code and trees load through the linker's source-index/fetch/admission (no resolver of your own); A is the only code identity; BLAKE3; no compat shims or version dispatch; lease/epoch/holder never enter a body; the de Bruijn kernels are backends with a documented fragment and are not widened (do not touch them).\n5\tDo: (0) F1: in `holder/driver_test`'s fence test assert the two `:yin.k/store` intents appear in journal order with `(:yin.k/record fence)` first and `(:yin.k/address fence)` second; F2: add the Q3 record-address case (`(assoc-in [:response :derivation :yin.ledger/profile :x] 1)` expecting `:install-image`) to `rows_custody_test`; (1) re-base `fencing_rows_test` (rows lift under header, `lower-task` with grant opts), `compose_test` (semantic-register `:receiver`/`:machine`; F3: replace `:export-version 99` in the smuggled-key test with `:source-index (fn [] {})`; the plain-composition test per the owner ruling), `compose_rows_test` (41 deftests; `offer-variant`-style helpers re-emit packs; content-store cuts see recovery v2 then the pack; the pack address is the store key and the root id inside the baseline), `handoff_v2_authority_test` (the 7a defect D1: it breaks under any option: re-base it on rows or delete it, state which and why: it tests the old inspector/codec which stays until phase 8, so prefer deleting only what tests the version-1/2 AUTHORITY path that no longer exists and keep whatever still tests the old codec directly); (2) the slow deftest `completion-recovery-unknown-policy-transaction-is-reconciled-once-test` under `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` re-based and green; (3) if production code needs a change to make these suites meaningful (compose.cljc seams, authority paths), make the smallest change and report it. If the plan and the code disagree, the code wins: report as a design defect, never silently change semantics. Portability: `.cljc` for JVM, Node, Dart (no `for` over possibly long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, no unary minus on floats, `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` order, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`); slow cases `^:slow` + `dao.test-slow/guard`.\n6\tVerification, ALL foreground, JVM only, never background a lane: `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>`; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched ns>` and `-i :slow` (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 where the suite uses it); every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace: report which still fail (only 7d's Stage E suites may remain red); `rows_test`, the harness, `layout_test` unchanged (no root id moves). No Node/Dart. Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify restore): recovery stored after the pack; a custody refusal after attach; a grant check skipped in the compose path; fencing lower without the exporting gate; offer carrying the wrong pack address; a content-store cut meaning swapped; source-index ignored in compose; report accepting an unfenced baseline. Which mutants do the tests catch? Do not commit. Report `collab/1792480000000-engineer-7c-compose-fencing.report.md`: files with line counts, test counts, mutants, deviations, design defects (separate list), what 7d needs.\n7\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306c61e-3078-4fbf-aeb8-718be5db0962","uuid":"1df10917-1b56-4e24-bde8-cab71ce78426","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:27:53.740Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c/collab/1792480000000-engineer-7c-compose-fencing.prompt.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 23:00 +07\n# Task: slice 7c, the composition and the compose and fencing rows (codex implements)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c`, branch `srvm-phase7c`, from the integration branch `srvm-phase7` (= master + 7a custody on rows + 7b holder export/recovery v2/driver lower/install checks). 7a-7d land on `srvm-phase7`; master only when 7d is green, so suites 7c/7d own are red until you re-base them. Your work will be reviewed by a NON-codex reviewer (Fable) with mutants: make every mutant below catchable by a test. Read first: `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`; `collab/phase7-plan.md` (3.4 crash cuts, 3.5 publication of successors, 3.6 authority vs sealed refs, 3.8, 3.9, section 4 slice 7c is your scope); `collab/7a-report.md`; `colla