breaks under any option: re-base it on rows or delete it, state which and why: it tests the old inspector/codec which stays until phase 8, so prefer deleting only what tests the version-1/2 AUTHORITY path that no longer exists and keep whatever still tests the old codec directly); (2) the slow deftest `completion-recovery-unknown-policy-transaction-is-reconciled-once-test` under `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` re-based and green; (3) if production code needs a change to make these suites meaningful (compose.cljc seams, authority paths), make the smallest change and report it. If the plan and the code disagree, the code wins: report as a design defect, never silently change semantics. Portability: `.cljc` for JVM, Node, Dart (no `for` over possibly long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, no unary minus on floats, `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` order, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`); slow cases `^:slow` + `dao.test-slow/guard`.\nVerification, ALL foreground, JVM only, never background a lane: `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>`; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched ns>` and `-i :slow` (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 where the suite uses it); every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace: report which still fail (only 7d's Stage E suites may remain red); `rows_test`, the harness, `layout_test` unchanged (no root id moves). No Node/Dart. Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify restore): recovery stored after the pack; a custody refusal after attach; a grant check skipped in the compose path; fencing lower without the exporting gate; offer carrying the wrong pack address; a content-store cut meaning swapped; source-index ignored in compose; report accepting an unfenced baseline. Which mutants do the tests catch? Do not commit. Report `collab/1792480000000-engineer-7c-compose-fencing.report.md`: files with line counts, test counts, mutants, deviations, design defects (separate list), what 7d needs.\n","numLines":7,"startLine":1,"totalLines":7}},"tool_r