{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NhU2FMBsbdb5rvdbXErHiZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-13 22:10 +07\n2\t# Review findings: slice 7b, the holder's export, recovery v2, the driver's lower, install checks\n3\t\n4\tReviewer: claude-fable-5-1 (non-author; codex wrote 7b, opus the retained partial edit). Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b`, branch `srvm-phase7b`, commit `95c228c0` over `srvm-phase7`. Method: full read of `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` (15 files), the plan (§3.2-3.5, 3.8, slice 7b), the 7a report, codex's 7b report and the brief; the quick and slow lanes of the named suites; a probe of the deferred suites; 18 mutants over `export.cljc`, `rows.cljc` and `driver.cljc` with byte-level restore verification. JVM only. Nothing in the repo was edited; review artifacts live under `target/7b-review/` (ignored).\n5\t\n6\t## Verification I ran\n7\t\n8\t| Lane | Command | Result |\n9\t|---|---|---|\n10\t| Quick | `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n` export, driver, writer, reader, evidence, rows-custody, rows-checkpoint, rows, safepoint-harness, layout, lift-v1, handoff-v2-holder | 329 tests, 7250 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n11\t| Slow | `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n` the ten suites of the brief | 5 tests, 3113 assertions, 0 failures |\n12\t| Lint | `clj -M:kondo --lint` the 12 changed `.cljc` files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n13\t| Probe | the deferred suites plus checkpoint, ledger-fixture, crash-cut, grant, completion, admission, store-write-audit | see below |\n14\t\n15\tSuites that stay red until 7c/7d (per `Testing` section of the probe log): `compose-rows-test` 39, `compose-test` 23, `fencing-rows-test` 31, `stage-e-rows-test` 5 (quick ones), `handoff-v2-authority-test` 8 (7a D1, needs an owner disposition). Every other probed suite is green: `checkpoint-test`, `ledger-fixture-test`, `crash-cut-test`, `authority.{grant,completion,admission}-test`, `store-write-audit-test`. This matches codex's table exactly; nothing else regressed.\n16\t\n17\t## What I checked, item by item\n18\t\n19\t1. **`holder/export.cljc`.** `prepare`/`encode` lift through `rows/lift-task` with `:header`, `:source-index` and `:serve-keyed` (`rows.cljc` threads the task path through `install-node` so child answers are keyed `[['host.mod] sid]`). `encode`'s server throws on an unprepared key and never calls `serve!`. D4 is honoured: the lift serves during the walk, the `once` closure records every answer before the lift's post-walk refusal, and a retry is seeded by handle from the retained table through the machine's bindings (`seeded-by-handle`), so no successful serve repeats (mutant M13 killed by four tests). Recovery v2 carries exactly `{export-recovery, version, pack-address, root, pack-bytes, header, state}`; `state` is `{gate origins issues issued children}` recursively. No snapshot body, no descriptor set, no lease/epoch/holder (the header's `:yin.k/origin` carries the predecessor's lease as lineage evidence, which the plan allows; the pack never carries `:yin.k/enrolled`, pinned by test). The deviation from the plan's sketch (no `:yin.k/descriptors`) follows the owner's \"only holder-local engine state beside the pack\" and is sound: rehydration rebuilds the served table from the attached descriptors.\n20\t2. **Rehydration.** Order in `rehydrate-fenced`: tag/version, recovery address, `checkpoint/inspect` (pack address vs bytes, carrier, custody grammar), root equality, `check-header!`, `header-agrees?` against the inspected custody, `valid-state?` against the decoded tree, then `lower-task {:fenced true}`. All before the first `attach` (tests pin `before = @attaches`). The fenced lower carries `id-counter` exactly (M03 killed, 68 assertions), builds `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids` from the census, moves waits and parked records out of the scheduler (M04 killed), gates every task `:exporting`; `extract-recovered` restamps issues and strips custody/closes/counters from the receiver. Zero program IO: M02d (ungated poll of the recovered waits) killed by six tests; M02b (rows-level fenced gate dropped) killed by `rows-custody-test` only, because `extract-recovered` re-asserts the gate itself (defence in depth, not a gap). `:make-stream` is nilled on a copy of the receiver passed to `spawn-module` and restored on the child; nothing is mutated, so there is no leak on exception. The recovered record re-encodes the published pack byte for byte (every rehydration test asserts `reproduces?`); a reordered-row pack of the same root is refused `:recovery-inconsistent`. Abort of a recovered record is refused `:restarted` (M05 killed).\n21\t3. **Q3 install checks.** `check-install!` requires `parent = (:yin.link/id response)` and a `:derivation` record whose address is the manifest's `:yin.semantic/code` entry, whose input is the manifest's tree and whose output is `segment-key` of the delivered image. The response shape (top-level `:manifest`, `:derivation`, `:image {:value}`) is exactly what `yin.vm.engine` reads at install (engine.cljc 1209, 1295, 1394) and what `linker/link-manifest` emits (`linked-image` merges `:manifest`, `:derivation`, `:trust` beside fetch's `:image`), so a valid linker-produced install is not refused; `:trusted` links also carry the record. A forged install passes only if manifest, record and image are mutually consistent: the check is self-consistency within the response, which is what the owner asked for (\"image address = the manifest's\"); binding the manifest to a composition-known address is the linker's admission, not the lower's. M06 and M07 (each check removed whole) killed; the three conjuncts of the image check separately: tree input (M07b) and image output (M07c) killed, record address (M07a, M07a2) **survived**, see F2.\n22\t4. **The driver.** `lowered` wraps `rows/lower-task` with the refusal-as-data contract; `lower` passes `:exclusive`, `:protection`, `:grant {:checkpoint address ...}`; `step-validating` inspects first, then lowers under `:exclusive` with no grant (awaiting-grant before any attachment; halted → `:safepoint` ended); `rebuilt-cell` checks `:yin.k/pack-address`, header equality, bytes vs base64 pack, then `rehydrate-fenced` and re-encode equality; `reopen-holder`/`reopen-exit` read kind/occurrence through the rows inspector. `:export-version` is gone from `driver.cljc` and `compose.cljc` (seam list, `bare-composition`, `driver-config`, docstrings); `source-index` is a required composition seam (`check!`) and a required driver seam. Occurrence minting and journaling precede prepare (unchanged `source-mint`/`exit-mint`); `export-fence-step` stores the recovery object first, then the pack (M11 **survived** at the test level, see F1); journal vocabulary unchanged, and renaming a journal tag or the store action (M12a/M12b) is refused by the driver's closed frame vocabulary so loudly that the test process cannot even load the suite (killed at process level).\n23\t5. **Deletions.** `lift_v1_test`: the five deleted deftests (`a-malformed-header…`, `two-encodes…`, `the-served-table…`, `a-retry-serves-no-already-served-handle…`, `the-record-round-trips…`) reappear verbatim in `export_test` over `rows_support` machines (`parked-writer-shared`/`-late` ported); the child-hold case now calls `export/enter` directly; `throws?` helper removed with them. `lift_support/prepared` removed and `lift` now calls `handoff/export-task` directly, so the old codec is exercised with no holder wrapper (codex D3, correct under \"no shims\"). `handoff_v2_holder_test`: only `a-version-2-recovery-snapshot-freezes-and-rehydrates-fenced` deleted, as the plan lists. `driver_test`: `a-version-two-fork-lift…` deleted as planned; `profile-refusal-precedes-wrong-address-test` becomes the two-address variant pinning profile-mismatch vs hash-mismatch with zero attaches. The old codec and inspector are untouched.\n24\t6. **`rows.cljc` and fixtures.** The 66 added lines are: `:serve-keyed`/`:path` plumbing (lift), the Q3 checks (stronger, not weaker), `with-custody`'s fenced parked move, `spawn-child`'s fenced constructor, the exact fenced `id-counter`, `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids`, and docstrings. `rows_support`: `linked-response` (manifest tree + derivation record, mirroring `link-manifest`), two shared-handle builders. The harness change is `module-response` data only. `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`: exactly three pins changed (`installs`, `child-header`, `child-op-id-out-of-range`), all install-bearing, as the extended install response requires; no other root moved (harness and `rows_test` green). `rows_custody_test` gains the Q3 deftest.\n25\t7. **Red suites**: listed above.\n26\t8. **Portability read.** No `for`, no private-var access across namespaces, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` everywhere new, `#?(:cljd … :clj …)` order kept, `(assoc {} …)` starts, no unary float minus, no EDN strings. Base64 through `jing/bytes->base64`/`base64->bytes` (the shared `dao.stream` codec, all hosts); byte equality by `(vec …)`; `integer?` on CBOR-decoded counters is host-safe for whole numbers. `yin.vm.engine/…` is never referenced from `export.cljc` (the surviving M02c mutant used it; the production file does not). `(:yin.link/id response)` and `parent` round-trip CBOR as vectors of keyword and int on every host. Unverified on Node/Dart by instruction.\n27\t\n28\t## Mutants (mine)\n29\t\n30\tDriver: `target/7b-review/mut.py`; each mutant's diff and log under `target/7b-review/mutants/`; restore verified by byte copy from a pristine backup plus `git diff --quiet -- src`; final `git status` shows no tracked change.\n31\t\n32\t| Mutant | Killed? | By |\n33\t|---|---|---|\n34\t| M01 freeze keeps a snapshot body | yes (1) | `the-recovery-object-is-the-pack-and-holder-local-state-test` |\n35\t| M02 rehydrate `vm/run`s the recovered machine (gated) | inert (0) | `vm/run` on a gated blocked machine does nothing; not a real mutant |\n36\t| M02b rows fenced gate and wait move dropped | yes (2) | `an-exclusive-blocked-root-under-fenced-skips-the-grant` only; export tests masked by `extract-recovered` |\n37\t| M02c rehydrate polls waits under gate `:running` | inert (0) | a gated machine observes nothing in `check-wait-set`; not a real mutant |\n38\t| M02d rehydrate polls the waits ungated (program IO) | yes (6) | the four zero-call rehydration tests, `complete-export-recovery…`, the FFI route test |\n39\t| M03 fenced id counter off by one | yes (68) | `the-id-counter-is-carried-exactly-test`, every `reproduces?` |\n40\t| M04 a parked record dropped at fenced lower | yes (14) | `recovery-retains-every-parked-record-test`, three more |\n41\t| M05 restarted abort accepted | yes (1) | `a-restarted-abort-is-refused-test` |\n42\t| M06 Q3 link-id check removed | yes (4) | `the-install-response-is-verified-before-any-attachment` |\n43\t| M07 Q3 image check removed whole | yes (10) | same |\n44\t| M07a / M07a2 Q3 record-address conjunct removed or weakened to `contains?` | **no** (0) | none: every \"another record\" case also changes the tree or the output |\n45\t| M07b Q3 tree-input conjunct removed | yes (2) | same deftest |\n46\t| M07c Q3 image-output conjunct removed | yes (4) | same deftest |\n47\t| M08 source index ignored (nil to the lift) | yes (91) | `the-lift-takes-trees-from-the-composition-source-index-test`, every lift |\n48\t| M09 attach before custody in `lower-task` | yes (30) | the four zero-attach deftests of `rows_custody_test` |\n49\t| M10 `:make-stream` not restored on a fenced child | **no** (0) | equivalent mutant: a fenced recovery never executes, so the child's constructor is never read |\n50\t| M11 recovery object stored after the pack | **no** (0) | no 7b suite observes the two-put order; only `compose_rows_test` (red until 7c) does |\n51\t| M12a journal tag `:yin.k/fenced` renamed | yes (process) | the driver's closed frame vocabulary throws at load |\n52\t| M12b store action `:yin.k/store` renamed | yes (process) | same |\n53\t| M13 serve repeated on retry (retained table and handle seed dropped) | yes (7) | `a-retry-serves-no-already-served-handle-test`, `a-refused-prepare-keeps-what-it-served-test`, two more |\n54\t\n55\tCodex's nine mutants are consistent with mine where they overlap (M01, M02d, M03, M04, M05, M06, M07, M08, M09).\n56\t\n57\t## Findings\n58\t\n59\t| id | severity | file:line | finding | fix |\n60\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n61\t| F1 | medium (test gap) | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:911` | The order \"recovery object first, then the pack\" is implemented but no green suite protects it: swapping the two `store-object` calls passes all 116 driver deftests (M11). Until 7c re-bases `compose_rows_test`, the crash-cut meaning of `store-put-*` vs `body-put-*` rests on reading the code. | In `driver_test`'s fence test (around line 3184) assert the two `:yin.k/store` intents appear in journal order with `(:yin.k/record fence)` first and `(:yin.k/address fence)` second. Five lines; can land with 7c. |\n62\t| F2 | low (test gap) | `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc:289` | The Q3 record-address conjunct (`segment-key record` = the manifest's `:yin.semantic/code` entry) is not isolated: replacing it with `(contains? manifest :yin.module/derivations)` passes (M07a2), because \"a derivation record the manifest does not name\" swaps in a record whose tree and output also differ, so the other conjuncts refuse first. | Add a case whose record keeps the honest input and output but differs in content (e.g. `(assoc-in [:response :derivation :yin.ledger/profile :x] 1)`), expecting `:install-image`. |\n63\t| F3 | low (7c note) | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:614` | The smuggled-key test still lists `:export-version 99` expecting the \"is a composition seam\" refusal; with the key removed from `holder-config-keys` this assertion will fail once 7c re-bases the suite. Not a 7b regression (the suite is red for other reasons) but it must not be mistaken for one. | 7c: replace the entry with `:source-index (fn [] {})`. |\n64\t| F4 | info | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:2074` | Restoring `:make-stream` on a fenced child is unobservable (M10): a fenced recovery never executes the child, and the relift does not read the constructor. Harmless hygiene; keep or drop. | None required. |\n65\t| F5 | info (design note) | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:1845` | The Q3 image check is self-consistency of manifest, record and image within the response; it does not bind the manifest to an address the composition knows, so a response that forges all three together passes. This is the owner's stated scope (link-id = parent, image = the manifest's) and admission stays the linker's; recorded so 7e documents the boundary. | 7e: say so in continuation §11 Q3's closing text. |\n66\t| F6 | info | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc:470` | `extract-recovered` re-asserts gate `:exporting` and an empty wait set, so `export_test` cannot see whether `rows/lower-task {:fenced true}` gated the tree (M02b was caught only by `rows_custody_test`). Defence in depth, acceptable; noted so nobody deletes the rows-level test as redundant. | None. |\n67\t\n68\tNo correctness defect found in the production code. The owner's rulings hold: A is the only code identity (trees from the composition's index, no resolver built), the AST is never lost (M08 refuses without the index), BLAKE3 for pack and recovery addresses, no version dispatch, no compat shim, lease/epoch/holder never in a body, fork custody nil, `yin.repl` untouched (it names `compose` only in docstrings).\n69\t\n70\tVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch `srvm-phase7`). F1 and F2 are test additions, non-blocking for integration; land them with 7c or as a small follow-up before 7c's review. F3 is 7c's.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306c61e-3078-4fbf-aeb8-718be5db0962","uuid":"b75ccd47-7184-42a1-a56c-8bb2c9dcda50","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:27:55.313Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c/collab/7b-review.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 22:10 +07\n# Review findings: slice 7b, the holder's export, recovery v2, the driver's lower, install checks\n\nReviewer: claude-fable-5-1 (non-author; codex wrote 7b, opus the retained partial edit). Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b`, branch `srvm-phase7b`, commit `95c228c0` over `srvm-phase7`. Method: full read of `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` (15 files), the plan (§3.2-3.5, 3.8, slice 7b), the 7a report, codex's 7b report and the brief; the quick and slow lanes of the named suites; a probe of the deferred suites; 18 mutants over `export.cljc`, `rows.cljc` and `driver.cljc` with byte-level restore verification. JVM only. Nothing in the repo was edited; review artifacts live under `target/7b-review/` (ignored).\n\n## Verification I ran\n\n| Lane | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quick | `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n` export, driver, writer, reader, evidence, rows-custody, rows-checkpoint, rows, safepoint-harness, layout, lift-v1, handoff-v2-holder | 329 tests, 7250 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Slow | `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n` the ten suites of the brief | 5 tests, 3113 assertions, 0 failures |\n| Lint | `clj -M:kondo --lint` the 12 changed `.cljc` files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Probe | the deferred suites plus checkpoint, ledger-fixture, crash-cut, grant, completion, admission, store-write-audit | see below |\n\nSuites that stay red until 7c/7d (per `Testing` section of the probe log): `compose-rows-test` 39, `compose-test` 23, `fencing-rows-test` 31, `stage-e-rows-test` 5 (quick ones), `handoff-v2-authority-test` 8 (7a D1, needs an owner disposition). Every other probed suite is green: `checkpoint-test`, `ledger-fixture-test`, `crash-cut-test`, `authority.{grant,completion,admission}-test`, `store-write-audit-test`. This matches codex's table exactly; nothing else regressed.\n\n## What I checked, item by item\n\n1. **`holder/export.cljc`.** `prepare`/`encode` lift through `rows/lift-task` with `:header`, `:source-index` and `:serve-keyed` (`rows.cljc` threads the task path through `install-node` so child answers are keyed `[['host.mod] sid]`). `encode`'s server throws on an unprepared key and never calls `serve!`. D4 is honoured: the lift serves during the walk, the `once` closure records every answer before the lift's post-walk refusal, and a retry is seeded by handle from the retained table through the machine's bindings (`seeded-by-handle`), so no successful serve repeats (mutant M13 killed by four tests). Recovery v2 carries exactly `{export-recovery, version, pack-address, root, pack-bytes, header, state}`; `state` is `{gate origins issues issued children}` recursively. No snapshot body, no descriptor set, no lease/epoch/holder (the header's `:yin.k/origin` carries the predecessor's lease as lineage evidence, which the plan allows; the pack never carries `:yin.k/enrolled`, pinned by test). The deviation from the plan's sketch (no `:yin.k/descriptors`) follows the owner's \"only holder-local engine state beside the pack\" and is sound: rehydration rebuilds the served table from the attached descriptors.\n2. **Rehydration.** Order in `rehydrate-fenced`: tag/version, recovery address, `checkpoint/inspect` (pack address vs bytes, carrier, custody grammar), root equality, `check-header!`, `header-agrees?` against the inspected custody, `valid-state?` against the decoded tree, then `lower-task {:fenced true}`. All before the first `attach` (tests pin `before = @attaches`). The fenced lower carries `id-counter` exactly (M03 killed, 68 assertions), builds `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids` from the census, moves waits and parked records out of the scheduler (M04 killed), gates every task `:exporting`; `extract-recovered` restamps issues and strips custody/closes/counters from the receiver. Zero program IO: M02d (ungated poll of the recovered waits) killed by six tests; M02b (rows-level fenced gate dropped) killed by `rows-custody-test` only, because `extract-recovered` re-asserts the gate itself (defence in depth, not a gap). `:make-stream` is nilled on a copy of the receiver passed to `spawn-module` and restored on the child; nothing is mutated, so there is no leak on exception. The recovered record re-encodes the published pack byte for byte (every rehydration test asserts `reproduces?`); a reordered-row pack of the same root is refused `:recovery-inconsistent`. Abort of a recovered record is refused `:restarted` (M05 killed).\n3. **Q3 install checks.** `check-install!` requires `parent = (:yin.link/id response)` and a `:derivation` record whose address is the manifest's `:yin.semantic/code` entry, whose input is the manifest's tree and whose output is `segment-key` of the delivered image. The response shape (top-level `:manifest`, `:derivation`, `:image {:value}`) is exactly what `yin.vm.engine` reads at install (engine.cljc 1209, 1295, 1394) and what `linker/link-manifest` emits (`linked-image` merges `:manifest`, `:derivation`, `:trust` beside fetch's `:image`), so a valid linker-produced install is not refused; `:trusted` links also carry the record. A forged install passes only if manifest, record and image are mutually consistent: the check is self-consistency within the response, which is what the owner asked for (\"image address = the manifest's\"); binding the manifest to a composition-known address is the linker's admission, not the lower's. M06 and M07 (each check removed whole) killed; the three conjuncts of the image check separately: tree input (M07b) and image output (M07c) killed, record address (M07a, M07a2) **survived**, see F2.\n4. **The driver.** `lowered` wraps `rows/lower-task` with the refusal-as-data contract; `lower` passes `:exclusive`, `:protection`, `:grant {:checkpoint address ...}`; `step-validating` inspects first, then lowers under `:exclusive` with no grant (awaiting-grant before any attachment; halted → `:safepoint` ended); `rebuilt-cell` checks `:yin.k/pack-address`, header equality, bytes vs base64 pack, then `rehydrate-fenced` and re-encode equality; `reopen-holder`/`reopen-exit` read kind/occurrence through the rows inspector. `:export-version` is gone from `driver.cljc` and `compose.cljc` (seam list, `bare-composition`, `driver-config`, docstrings); `source-index` is a required composition seam (`check!`) and a required driver seam. Occurrence minting and journaling precede prepare (unchanged `source-mint`/`exit-mint`); `export-fence-step` stores the recovery object first, then the pack (M11 **survived** at the test level, see F1); journal vocabulary unchanged, and renaming a journal tag or the store action (M12a/M12b) is refused by the driver's closed frame vocabulary so loudly that the test process cannot even load the suite (killed at process level).\n5. **Deletions.** `lift_v1_test`: the five deleted deftests (`a-malformed-header…`, `two-encodes…`, `the-served-table…`, `a-retry-serves-no-already-served-handle…`, `the-record-round-trips…`) reappear verbatim in `export_test` over `rows_support` machines (`parked-writer-shared`/`-late` ported); the child-hold case now calls `export/enter` directly; `throws?` helper removed with them. `lift_support/prepared` removed and `lift` now calls `handoff/export-task` directly, so the old codec is exercised with no holder wrapper (codex D3, correct under \"no shims\"). `handoff_v2_holder_test`: only `a-version-2-recovery-snapshot-freezes-and-rehydrates-fenced` deleted, as the plan lists. `driver_test`: `a-version-two-fork-lift…` deleted as planned; `profile-refusal-precedes-wrong-address-test` becomes the two-address variant pinning profile-mismatch vs hash-mismatch with zero attaches. The old codec and inspector are untouched.\n6. **`rows.cljc` and fixtures.** The 66 added lines are: `:serve-keyed`/`:path` plumbing (lift), the Q3 checks (stronger, not weaker), `with-custody`'s fenced parked move, `spawn-child`'s fenced constructor, the exact fenced `id-counter`, `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids`, and docstrings. `rows_support`: `linked-response` (manifest tree + derivation record, mirroring `link-manifest`), two shared-handle builders. The harness change is `module-response` data only. `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`: exactly three pins changed (`installs`, `child-header`, `child-op-id-out-of-range`), all install-bearing, as the extended install response requires; no other root moved (harness and `rows_test` green). `rows_custody_test` gains the Q3 deftest.\n7. **Red suites**: listed above.\n8. **Portability read.** No `for`, no private-var access across namespaces, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` everywhere new, `#?(:cljd … :clj …)` order kept, `(assoc {} …)` starts, no unary float minus, no EDN strings. Base64 through `jing/bytes->base64`/`base64->bytes` (the shared `dao.stream` codec, all hosts); byte equality by `(vec …)`; `integer?` on CBOR-decoded counters is host-safe for whole numbers. `yin.vm.engine/…` is never referenced from `export.cljc` (the surviving M02c mutant used it; the production file does not). `(:yin.link/id response)` and `parent` round-trip CBOR as vectors of keyword and int on every host. Unverified on Node/Dart by instruction.\n\n## Mutants (mine)\n\nDriver: `target/7b-review/mut.py`; each mutant's diff and log under `target/7b-review/mutants/`; restore verified by byte copy from a pristine backup plus `git diff --quiet -- src`; final `git status` shows no tracked change.\n\n| Mutant | Killed? | By |\n|---|---|---|\n| M01 freeze keeps a snapshot body | yes (1) | `the-recovery-object-is-the-pack-and-holder-local-state-test` |\n| M02 rehydrate `vm/run`s the recovered machine (gated) | inert (0) | `vm/run` on a gated blocked machine does nothing; not a real mutant |\n| M02b rows fenced gate and wait move dropped | yes (2) | `an-exclusive-blocked-root-under-fenced-skips-the-grant` only; export tests masked by `extract-recovered` |\n| M02c rehydrate polls waits under gate `:running` | inert (0) | a gated machine observes nothing in `check-wait-set`; not a real mutant |\n| M02d rehydrate polls the waits ungated (program IO) | yes (6) | the four zero-call rehydration tests, `complete-export-recovery…`, the FFI route test |\n| M03 fenced id counter off by one | yes (68) | `the-id-counter-is-carried-exactly-test`, every `reproduces?` |\n| M04 a parked record dropped at fenced lower | yes (14) | `recovery-retains-every-parked-record-test`, three more |\n| M05 restarted abort accepted | yes (1) | `a-restarted-abort-is-refused-test` |\n| M06 Q3 link-id check removed | yes (4) | `the-install-response-is-verified-before-any-attachment` |\n| M07 Q3 image check removed whole | yes (10) | same |\n| M07a / M07a2 Q3 record-address conjunct removed or weakened to `contains?` | **no** (0) | none: every \"another record\" case also changes the tree or the output |\n| M07b Q3 tree-input conjunct removed | yes (2) | same deftest |\n| M07c Q3 image-output conjunct removed | yes (4) | same deftest |\n| M08 source index ignored (nil to the lift) | yes (91) | `the-lift-takes-trees-from-the-composition-source-index-test`, every lift |\n| M09 attach before custody in `lower-task` | yes (30) | the four zero-attach deftests of `rows_custody_test` |\n| M10 `:make-stream` not restored on a fenced child | **no** (0) | equivalent mutant: a fenced recovery never executes, so the child's constructor is never read |\n| M11 recovery object stored after the pack | **no** (0) | no 7b suite observes the two-put order; only `compose_rows_test` (red until 7c) does |\n| M12a journal tag `:yin.k/fenced` renamed | yes (process) | the driver's closed frame vocabulary throws at load |\n| M12b store action `:yin.k/store` renamed | yes (process) | same |\n| M13 serve repeated on retry (retained table and handle seed dropped) | yes (7) | `a-retry-serves-no-already-served-handle-test`, `a-refused-prepare-keeps-what-it-served-test`, two more |\n\nCodex's nine mutants are consistent with mine where they overlap (M01, M02d, M03, M04, M05, M06, M07, M08, M09).\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | severity | file:line | finding | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | medium (test gap) | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:911` | The order \"recovery object first, then the pack\" is implemented but no green suite protects it: swapping the two `store-object` calls passes all 116 driver deftests (M11). Until 7c re-bases `compose_rows_test`, the crash-cut meaning of `store-put-*` vs `body-put-*` rests on reading the code. | In `driver_test`'s fence test (around line 3184) assert the two `:yin.k/store` intents appear in journal order with `(:yin.k/record fence)` first and `(:yin.k/address fence)` second. Five lines; can land with 7c. |\n| F2 | low (test gap) | `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc:289` | The Q3 record-address conjunct (`segment-key record` = the manifest's `:yin.semantic/code` entry) is not isolated: replacing it with `(contains? manifest :yin.module/derivations)` passes (M07a2), because \"a derivation record the manifest does not name\" swaps in a record whose tree and output also differ, so the other conjuncts refuse first. | Add a case whose record keeps the honest input and output but differs in content (e.g. `(assoc-in [:response :derivation :yin.ledger/profile :x] 1)`), expecting `:install-image`. |\n| F3 | low (7c note) | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:614` | The smuggled-key test still lists `:export-version 99` expecting the \"is a composition seam\" refusal; with the key removed from `holder-config-keys` this assertion will fail once 7c re-bases the suite. Not a 7b regression (the suite is red for other reasons) but it must not be mistaken for one. | 7c: replace the entry with `:source-index (fn [] {})`. |\n| F4 | info | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:2074` | Restoring `:make-stream` on a fenced child is unobservable (M10): a fenced recovery never executes the child, and the relift does not read the constructor. Harmless hygiene; keep or drop. | None required. |\n| F5 | info (design note) | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:1845` | The Q3 image check is self-consistency of manifest, record and image within the response; it does not bind the manifest to an address the composition knows, so a response that forges all three together passes. This is the owner's stated scope (link-id = parent, image = the manifest's) and admission stays the linker's; recorded so 7e documents the boundary. | 7e: say so in continuation §11 Q3's closing text. |\n| F6 | info | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc:470` | `extract-recovered` re-asserts gate `:exporting` and an empty wait set, so `export_test` cannot see whether `rows/lower-task {:fenced true}` gated the tree (M02b was caught only by `rows_custody_test`). Defence in depth, acceptable; noted so nobody deletes the rows-level test as redundant. | None. |\n\nNo correctness defect found in the production code. The owner's rulings hold: A is the only code identity (trees from the composition's index, no resolver built), the AST is never lost (M08 refuses without the index), BLAKE3 for pack and recovery addresses, no version dispatch, no compat shim, lease/epoch/holder never in a body, fork custody nil, `yin.repl` untouched (it names `compose` only in docstrings).\n\nVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch `srvm-phase7`). F1 and F2 are test additions, non-blocking for integration; land them with 7c or as a small follow-up before 7c's review. F3 is 7c's.\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NhU2FMBsbdb5rvdbXErHiZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
