{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wMAL5DAbU424g8rF54qou","type":"tool_result","content":"2233\t\n2234\t\n2235\t(defn lower-task\n2236\t  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n2237\t   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n2238\t   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n2239\t   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n2240\t   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n2241\t   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n2242\t   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n2243\t   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n2244\t   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n2245\t   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n2246\t   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n2247\t   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n2248\t   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n2249\t   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n2250\t   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n2251\t   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n2252\t   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\"\n2253\t  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n2254\t  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n2255\t   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n2256\t     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n2257\t     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n2258\t     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n2259\t             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n2260\t       (step recv t role))\n2261\t     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n2262\t       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))\n2263\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306c61e-3078-4fbf-aeb8-718be5db0962","uuid":"0ddfc54b-32d3-4a61-9b0d-b8f5ea331e88","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:29:11.447Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc","content":"\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n       (step recv t role))\n     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))\n","numLines":31,"startLine":2233,"totalLines":2263}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016wMAL5DAbU424g8rF54qou","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
