{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018C4EYpe4dikpGDs7ZJeebV","type":"tool_result","content":"85\t  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/succeeded\n86\t   :yin.k/occurrence o\n87\t   :yin.k/result address})\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t;; =============================================================================\n91\t;; The report\n92\t;; =============================================================================\n93\t\n94\t(defn- successor-defect\n95\t  \"Why baseline `b` is not a successor of occurrence `o` under lease `l`\n96\t   against projection p, or nil.  A halted result is checked only for\n97\t   its origin: it carries no occurrence, arbitration or counter.\"\n98\t  [p o l b]\n99\t  (let [s (:yin.k/occurrence b)]\n100\t    (cond\n101\t      (not (and (= o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence]))\n102\t                (= l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease]))))\n103\t      :wrong-origin\n104\t      (= :halted (:yin.k/kind b)) nil\n105\t      (not= (:arbitration p)\n106\t            (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n107\t      :foreign-arbitration\n108\t      (ledger/successor-seen? p s) :seen-occurrence\n109\t      (neg? (cbor/num-compare\n110\t              (:yin.k/next-op-seq b)\n111\t              (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/baseline :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n112\t      :counter-regression\n113\t      :else nil)))\n114\t\n115\t\n116\t(defn- refused\n117\t  [reason]\n118\t  {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason reason}})\n119\t\n120\t\n121\t(defn- report-decision\n122\t  [author report b]\n123\t  (fn [p]\n124\t    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence report)\n125\t          l (:dao.lease/lease report)\n126\t          address (:yin.k/result report)\n127\t          entry (get-in p [:leases l])]\n128\t      (cond\n129\t        (nil? entry) (refused :unknown-lease)\n130\t        (not= o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)) (refused :wrong-occurrence)\n131\t        (not= author (:dao.lease/holder entry)) (refused :not-holder)\n132\t        (= address (:yin.k/result entry))\n133\t        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed}}\n134\t        (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause) (refused :ended-lease)\n135\t        (contains? entry :yin.k/result) (refused :report-conflict)\n136\t        (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]) (refused :quarantined)\n137\t        :else\n138\t        (if-let [d (successor-defect p o l b)]\n139\t          (refused d)\n140\t          {::authority/facts [(cond-> report\n141\t                                (not= :halted (:yin.k/kind b))\n142\t                                (assoc :yin.k/successor\n143\t                                       (:yin.k/occurrence b)))]\n144\t           ::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :committed}})))))\n145\t\n146\t\n147\t(defn report!\n148\t  \"Admit holder `author`'s report `report` (a `resumed` fact) of the\n149\t   successor whose canonical bytes are `bytes`.  Answers\n150\t\n151\t     {:yin.k/status :committed :dao.space/t t}\n152\t     {:yin.k/status :replayed}                 ; the recorded report\n153\t     {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason r}\n154\t\n155\t   with r one of :malformed-report, :uninspectable (carrying the\n156\t   inspector's refusal under `:yin.k/inspection`), :unknown-lease,\n157\t   :wrong-occurrence, :not-holder, :ended-lease, :report-conflict\n158\t   (another report for the lease), :quarantined, :wrong-origin,\n159\t   :foreign-arbitration, :seen-occurrence and :counter-regression (the\n160\t   last three never for a halted result); or the authority's own\n161\t   :suspended and :closed answers.  A refused report writes nothing.\"\n162\t  [a author report bytes]\n163\t  (if-not (and (map? report)\n164\t               (= #{:yin.k/custody :yin.k/occurrence :dao.lease/lease\n165\t                    :yin.k/result}\n166\t                  (set (keys report)))\n167\t               (= :yin.k/resumed (:yin.k/custody report))\n168\t               (custody/occurrence? (:yin.k/occurrence report))\n169\t               (some? (:dao.lease/lease report)))\n170\t    {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :malformed-report}\n171\t    (let [b (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/result report) bytes)]\n172\t      (if (contains? b :yin.k/status)\n173\t        {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :uninspectable\n174\t         :yin.k/inspection b}\n175\t        (authority/transition! a (report-decision author report b))))))\n176\t\n177\t\n178\t;; =============================================================================\n179\t;; Completion, in the release or policy lapse's transaction\n180\t;; =============================================================================\n181\t\n182\t(defn closure\n183\t  \"The facts that complete the occurrence of lapse fact `f` against\n184\t   projection p: its closure and its one edge, when f is a `:release` or `:policy`\n185\t   lapse of a live, reported lease on an unquarantined occurrence whose\n186\t   reclaim does not exhaust it, and whose successor, if the report named\n187\t   a continuation, the ledger has not seen; else none.  The edge goes to\n188\t   the successor occurrence, or for a halted result is the terminal edge\n189\t   to its address.  They belong between the lapse and its epoch change.\"\n190\t  [p f]\n191\t  (let [l (:dao.lease/lease f)\n192\t        entry (get-in p [:leases l])\n193\t        o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)\n194\t        s (:yin.k/successor entry)]\n195\t    (if (and (contains? #{:release :policy} (:dao.lease/cause f))\n196\t             (contains? entry :yin.k/result)\n197\t             (not (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause))\n198\t             (= l (get-in p [:occurrences o :dao.lease/lease]))\n199\t             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed]))\n200\t             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]))\n201\t             (not= (:max-epoch p) (:yin.k/epoch entry))\n202\t             (not (and (some? s) (ledger/successor-seen? p s))))\n203\t      [(completed o l)\n204\t       (if (some? s) (succeeded o s) (terminated o (:yin.k/result entry)))]\n205\t      [])))\n206\t\n207\t\n208\t;; =============================================================================\n209\t;; Successor offers\n210\t;; =============================================================================\n211\t\n212\t(defn offer-refusal\n213\t  \"Why the first offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` may not be\n214\t   admitted against projection p, or nil.  A body with no origin, a\n215\t   first export, is unconstrained.  A body with an origin must be the\n216\t   successor its predecessor's closure recorded in this ledger, under\n217\t   the closing lease, at the reported address.  :awaiting-completion\n218\t   while the origin's lease is the live one; :orphan otherwise,\n219\t   including a predecessor this ledger never saw (7.7.8: a successor's\n220\t   arbitration is its predecessor's, unchanged).\"\n221\t  [p address b]\n222\t  (let [o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence])\n223\t        l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease])\n224\t        pred (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n225\t        closed (:yin.k/closed pred)]\n226\t    (cond\n227\t      (not (contains? b :yin.k/origin)) nil\n228\t      (nil? pred) :orphan\n229\t      (nil? closed)\n230\t      (if (= l (:dao.lease/lease pred)) :awaiting-completion :orphan)\n231\t      (and (= l (:dao.lease/lease closed))\n232\t           (= (:yin.k/occurrence b) (:yin.k/successor closed))\n233\t           (= address (get-in p [:leases l :yin.k/result])))\n234\t      nil"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306c61e-3078-4fbf-aeb8-718be5db0962","uuid":"2ea4b2b3-dbd9-4f76-8b0d-c6875e6248f8","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:29:12.254Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/completion.cljc","content":"  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/succeeded\n   :yin.k/occurrence o\n   :yin.k/result address})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The report\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- successor-defect\n  \"Why baseline `b` is not a successor of occurrence `o` under lease `l`\n   against projection p, or nil.  A halted result is checked only for\n   its origin: it carries no occurrence, arbitration or counter.\"\n  [p o l b]\n  (let [s (:yin.k/occurrence b)]\n    (cond\n      (not (and (= o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence]))\n                (= l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease]))))\n      :wrong-origin\n      (= :halted (:yin.k/kind b)) nil\n      (not= (:arbitration p)\n            (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n      :foreign-arbitration\n      (ledger/successor-seen? p s) :seen-occurrence\n      (neg? (cbor/num-compare\n              (:yin.k/next-op-seq b)\n              (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/baseline :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n      :counter-regression\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn- refused\n  [reason]\n  {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason reason}})\n\n\n(defn- report-decision\n  [author report b]\n  (fn [p]\n    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence report)\n          l (:dao.lease/lease report)\n          address (:yin.k/result report)\n          entry (get-in p [:leases l])]\n      (cond\n        (nil? entry) (refused :unknown-lease)\n        (not= o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)) (refused :wrong-occurrence)\n        (not= author (:dao.lease/holder entry)) (refused :not-holder)\n        (= address (:yin.k/result entry))\n        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed}}\n        (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause) (refused :ended-lease)\n        (contains? entry :yin.k/result) (refused :report-conflict)\n        (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]) (refused :quarantined)\n        :else\n        (if-let [d (successor-defect p o l b)]\n          (refused d)\n          {::authority/facts [(cond-> report\n                                (not= :halted (:yin.k/kind b))\n                                (assoc :yin.k/successor\n                                       (:yin.k/occurrence b)))]\n           ::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :committed}})))))\n\n\n(defn report!\n  \"Admit holder `author`'s report `report` (a `resumed` fact) of the\n   successor whose canonical bytes are `bytes`.  Answers\n\n     {:yin.k/status :committed :dao.space/t t}\n     {:yin.k/status :replayed}                 ; the recorded report\n     {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason r}\n\n   with r one of :malformed-report, :uninspectable (carrying the\n   inspector's refusal under `:yin.k/inspection`), :unknown-lease,\n   :wrong-occurrence, :not-holder, :ended-lease, :report-conflict\n   (another report for the lease), :quarantined, :wrong-origin,\n   :foreign-arbitration, :seen-occurrence and :counter-regression (the\n   last three never for a halted result); or the authority's own\n   :suspended and :closed answers.  A refused report writes nothing.\"\n  [a author report bytes]\n  (if-not (and (map? report)\n               (= #{:yin.k/custody :yin.k/occurrence :dao.lease/lease\n                    :yin.k/result}\n                  (set (keys report)))\n               (= :yin.k/resumed (:yin.k/custody report))\n               (custody/occurrence? (:yin.k/occurrence report))\n               (some? (:dao.lease/lease report)))\n    {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :malformed-report}\n    (let [b (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/result report) bytes)]\n      (if (contains? b :yin.k/status)\n        {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :uninspectable\n         :yin.k/inspection b}\n        (authority/transition! a (report-decision author report b))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Completion, in the release or policy lapse's transaction\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn closure\n  \"The facts that complete the occurrence of lapse fact `f` against\n   projection p: its closure and its one edge, when f is a `:release` or `:policy`\n   lapse of a live, reported lease on an unquarantined occurrence whose\n   reclaim does not exhaust it, and whose successor, if the report named\n   a continuation, the ledger has not seen; else none.  The edge goes to\n   the successor occurrence, or for a halted result is the terminal edge\n   to its address.  They belong between the lapse and its epoch change.\"\n  [p f]\n  (let [l (:dao.lease/lease f)\n        entry (get-in p [:leases l])\n        o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)\n        s (:yin.k/successor entry)]\n    (if (and (contains? #{:release :policy} (:dao.lease/cause f))\n             (contains? entry :yin.k/result)\n             (not (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause))\n             (= l (get-in p [:occurrences o :dao.lease/lease]))\n             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed]))\n             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]))\n             (not= (:max-epoch p) (:yin.k/epoch entry))\n             (not (and (some? s) (ledger/successor-seen? p s))))\n      [(completed o l)\n       (if (some? s) (succeeded o s) (terminated o (:yin.k/result entry)))]\n      [])))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Successor offers\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn offer-refusal\n  \"Why the first offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` may not be\n   admitted against projection p, or nil.  A body with no origin, a\n   first export, is unconstrained.  A body with an origin must be the\n   successor its predecessor's closure recorded in this ledger, under\n   the closing lease, at the reported address.  :awaiting-completion\n   while the origin's lease is the live one; :orphan otherwise,\n   including a predecessor this ledger never saw (7.7.8: a successor's\n   arbitration is its predecessor's, unchanged).\"\n  [p address b]\n  (let [o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence])\n        l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease])\n        pred (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n        closed (:yin.k/closed pred)]\n    (cond\n      (not (contains? b :yin.k/origin)) nil\n      (nil? pred) :orphan\n      (nil? closed)\n      (if (= l (:dao.lease/lease pred)) :awaiting-completion :orphan)\n      (and (= l (:dao.lease/lease closed))\n           (= (:yin.k/occurrence b) (:yin.k/successor closed))\n           (= address (get-in p [:leases l :yin.k/result])))\n      nil","numLines":150,"startLine":85,"totalLines":236}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018C4EYpe4dikpGDs7ZJeebV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
