{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mic34kLVtnpbM8hUqP72FR","type":"tool_result","content":"95\t(def front-budget\n96\t  \"How many requests one front step reads, the same bound the driver\n97\t   suites drive their fronts with.\"\n98\t  16)\n99\t\n100\t\n101\t(defn- check!\n102\t  [ok what data]\n103\t  (when-not ok\n104\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"The custody composition needs \" what)\n105\t                    (into {} (cons {:yin.k/hint :assembly} data))))))\n106\t\n107\t\n108\t(defn- check-interval!\n109\t  \"The renewal interval gate the driver runs at its own assembly, run\n110\t   here so an unsizable composition refuses at open, before any medium\n111\t   is minted.\"\n112\t  [units interval]\n113\t  (check! (lease/duration? interval)\n114\t          \"a renewal interval: a single-entry {unit positive-integer} map\"\n115\t          {:renewal-interval interval})\n116\t  (let [[unit magnitude] (first interval)]\n117\t    (check! (some? (get units unit))\n118\t            \"a renewal interval whose unit is in the unit table\"\n119\t            {:renewal-interval interval :units units})\n120\t    (check! (<= magnitude (quot lease/magnitude-limit (get units unit)))\n121\t            \"a renewal interval within the per-unit bound\"\n122\t            {:renewal-interval interval})))\n123\t\n124\t\n125\t(defn- check-substrate!\n126\t  \"The shape gate for a fork composition's optional substrate (an\n127\t   exclusive composition validates :journals as a data refusal instead,\n128\t   in exclusive-journals-refusal): nil, or a map whose two suppliers are\n129\t   functions.\"\n130\t  [{:keys [journals]}]\n131\t  (check! (or (nil? journals)\n132\t              (and (map? journals)\n133\t                   (every? fn? (keep journals [:progress-backend! :reply-backend!]))))\n134\t          \"a journal substrate: nil, or {:progress-backend! f :reply-backend! f} over (fn [holder] backend) -- file-journals for production, memory-journals for tests\"\n135\t          {:journals journals}))\n136\t\n137\t\n138\t(def ^:private failure-rank\n139\t  {:none 0 :process-crash 1 :power-loss 2})\n140\t\n141\t\n142\t(defn- journal-substrate-capable?\n143\t  \"True only when a journal substrate's declared durability can carry an\n144\t   exclusive composition that requires surviving `required`: its backend\n145\t   is :file and its declared failure model covers `required` (a file\n146\t   journal declares :process-crash, a memory journal :none).  Nil\n147\t   durability -- a substrate that declares nothing -- is never capable.\"\n148\t  [durability required]\n149\t  (and (contains? #{:process-crash :power-loss} required)\n150\t       (= :file (:dao.stream.journal/backend durability))\n151\t       (<= (failure-rank required)\n152\t           (get failure-rank (:dao.stream.journal/failure-model durability)\n153\t                0))))\n154\t\n155\t\n156\t(defn- exclusive-journals-refusal\n157\t  \"The data refusal for an exclusive composition whose :journals cannot\n158\t   carry its declared failure model: nil, an empty or partial substrate\n159\t   (missing either supplier), or a substrate whose declared durability is\n160\t   insufficient -- a memory substrate (:none) or a file substrate asked\n161\t   to survive :power-loss.  Nil when the substrate is acceptable.  This\n162\t   is the composition's data refusal, beside :exclusive-uncapable, never\n163\t   a silent substitution of memory storage.\"\n164\t  [{:keys [journals failure-model]}]\n165\t  (let [durability (when (map? journals)\n166\t                     (:dao.stream.journal/durability journals))]\n167\t    (when (or (nil? journals)\n168\t              (not (and (fn? (:progress-backend! journals))\n169\t                        (fn? (:reply-backend! journals))))\n170\t              (not (journal-substrate-capable? durability failure-model)))\n171\t      {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\n172\t       :yin.k/reason :journals-uncapable\n173\t       :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive\n174\t       :yin.k/failure-model failure-model\n175\t       :dao.stream.journal/durability durability})))\n176\t\n177\t\n178\t(defn- check-common!\n179\t  [config]\n180\t  (check-interval! (:units config) (:renewal-interval config))\n181\t  (check! (and (map? (:store config))\n182\t               (fn? (:put-bytes-fn (:store config)))\n183\t               (fn? (:get-bytes-fn (:store config))))\n184\t          \"a content store: a dao.jing byte-store handle\" {})\n185\t  (check! (some? (:diagnostics config)) \"a diagnostic stream: a writer\" {})\n186\t  (check! (some? (:medium config)) \"a carrier medium name\" {})\n187\t  (check! (fn? (:clock config)) \"a lease clock: (fn [] reading)\" {})\n188\t  (check! (fn? (:source-index config))\n189\t          \"a source index: (fn [] {A #{tree-address}})\" {}))\n190\t\n191\t\n192\t(defn- log-handle\n193\t  \"A fresh memory log: the composition's tick and lease-fact media.\"\n194\t  []\n195\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n196\t    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n197\t\n198\t\n199\t(defn- ring-handle\n200\t  [capacity]\n201\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n202\t    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n203\t                   ring/capacity-key capacity})))\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306c61e-3078-4fbf-aeb8-718be5db0962","uuid":"7b9c356b-3887-45cc-b10d-2cf033606f37","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:29:46.945Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/compose.cljc","content":"(def front-budget\n  \"How many requests one front step reads, the same bound the driver\n   suites drive their fronts with.\"\n  16)\n\n\n(defn- check!\n  [ok what data]\n  (when-not ok\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"The custody composition needs \" what)\n                    (into {} (cons {:yin.k/hint :assembly} data))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-interval!\n  \"The renewal interval gate the driver runs at its own assembly, run\n   here so an unsizable composition refuses at open, before any medium\n   is minted.\"\n  [units interval]\n  (check! (lease/duration? interval)\n          \"a renewal interval: a single-entry {unit positive-integer} map\"\n          {:renewal-interval interval})\n  (let [[unit magnitude] (first interval)]\n    (check! (some? (get units unit))\n            \"a renewal interval whose unit is in the unit table\"\n            {:renewal-interval interval :units units})\n    (check! (<= magnitude (quot lease/magnitude-limit (get units unit)))\n            \"a renewal interval within the per-unit bound\"\n            {:renewal-interval interval})))\n\n\n(defn- check-substrate!\n  \"The shape gate for a fork composition's optional substrate (an\n   exclusive composition validates :journals as a data refusal instead,\n   in exclusive-journals-refusal): nil, or a map whose two suppliers are\n   functions.\"\n  [{:keys [journals]}]\n  (check! (or (nil? journals)\n              (and (map? journals)\n                   (every? fn? (keep journals [:progress-backend! :reply-backend!]))))\n          \"a journal substrate: nil, or {:progress-backend! f :reply-backend! f} over (fn [holder] backend) -- file-journals for production, memory-journals for tests\"\n          {:journals journals}))\n\n\n(def ^:private failure-rank\n  {:none 0 :process-crash 1 :power-loss 2})\n\n\n(defn- journal-substrate-capable?\n  \"True only when a journal substrate's declared durability can carry an\n   exclusive composition that requires surviving `required`: its backend\n   is :file and its declared failure model covers `required` (a file\n   journal declares :process-crash, a memory journal :none).  Nil\n   durability -- a substrate that declares nothing -- is never capable.\"\n  [durability required]\n  (and (contains? #{:process-crash :power-loss} required)\n       (= :file (:dao.stream.journal/backend durability))\n       (<= (failure-rank required)\n           (get failure-rank (:dao.stream.journal/failure-model durability)\n                0))))\n\n\n(defn- exclusive-journals-refusal\n  \"The data refusal for an exclusive composition whose :journals cannot\n   carry its declared failure model: nil, an empty or partial substrate\n   (missing either supplier), or a substrate whose declared durability is\n   insufficient -- a memory substrate (:none) or a file substrate asked\n   to survive :power-loss.  Nil when the substrate is acceptable.  This\n   is the composition's data refusal, beside :exclusive-uncapable, never\n   a silent substitution of memory storage.\"\n  [{:keys [journals failure-model]}]\n  (let [durability (when (map? journals)\n                     (:dao.stream.journal/durability journals))]\n    (when (or (nil? journals)\n              (not (and (fn? (:progress-backend! journals))\n                        (fn? (:reply-backend! journals))))\n              (not (journal-substrate-capable? durability failure-model)))\n      {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\n       :yin.k/reason :journals-uncapable\n       :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive\n       :yin.k/failure-model failure-model\n       :dao.stream.journal/durability durability})))\n\n\n(defn- check-common!\n  [config]\n  (check-interval! (:units config) (:renewal-interval config))\n  (check! (and (map? (:store config))\n               (fn? (:put-bytes-fn (:store config)))\n               (fn? (:get-bytes-fn (:store config))))\n          \"a content store: a dao.jing byte-store handle\" {})\n  (check! (some? (:diagnostics config)) \"a diagnostic stream: a writer\" {})\n  (check! (some? (:medium config)) \"a carrier medium name\" {})\n  (check! (fn? (:clock config)) \"a lease clock: (fn [] reading)\" {})\n  (check! (fn? (:source-index config))\n          \"a source index: (fn [] {A #{tree-address}})\" {}))\n\n\n(defn- log-handle\n  \"A fresh memory log: the composition's tick and lease-fact media.\"\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n\n\n(defn- ring-handle\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                   ring/capacity-key capacity})))\n","numLines":110,"startLine":95,"totalLines":1010}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Mic34kLVtnpbM8hUqP72FR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
