{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kqv5rR2YVnX3CmZciBkwsV","type":"tool_result","content":"238\t\n239\t\n240\t(defn- holder-seams\n241\t  \"The holder's own seams over program identity `p`.\"\n242\t  [p attach-table]\n243\t  {:protection {p :at-least-once}\n244\t   :receiver (s/new-machine)\n245\t   :attach! (attach-over attach-table)\n246\t   :observe! (observe-over)\n247\t   :serve! (serve-as p)})\n248\t\n249\t\n250\t(defn fork-world\n251\t  \"A fork composition (the caller's selection) over one source machine.\n252\t  No authority, no judge, no fronts: the composition's own decision.\n253\t  Public: the no-yin.repl subprocess drives it.\"\n254\t  []\n255\t  (compose/open! {:source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n256\t                  :mode :fork\n257\t                  :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n258\t                  :store (mem/create-content-mem)\n259\t                  :diagnostics (log-writer)\n260\t                  :medium \"compose-test\"\n261\t                  :clock (fn [] {:s 1})}))\n262\t\n263\t\n264\t(defn driven-fork-composition\n265\t  \"A fork composition whose single source has run to its :lifted answer:\n266\t  the whole drive a fresh process performs in the no-yin.repl row.\"\n267\t  []\n268\t  (let [c (get (fork-world) ::compose/composition)\n269\t        c (compose/source c \"h1\"\n270\t                          (merge (holder-seams \"prog-f\" {\"prog-f\" (int-stream \"prog-f\")})\n271\t                                 {:machine (parked-reader-over (int-stream \"prog-f\"))}))]\n272\t    (drive c \"h1\" (phase-of :lifted) 8)))\n273\t\n274\t\n275\t(defn exclusive-world\n276\t  \"An exclusive composition over a file-backed authority (the backend\n277\t  that passes the gate for :process-crash) in a fresh scratch directory,\n278\t  one source holder over a real parked machine, its journals on a\n279\t  file-backed substrate over a scratch root of its own.  The receiver\n280\t  attaches its own instance of the program stream, the instance the run\n281\t  reads; `:attaches` counts its attach calls.  `:inbound` overrides the\n282\t  composition's ring -- the bounded medium the drain rows supply;\n283\t  `:journals` overrides the composition's journal substrate (the stable\n284\t  recovery configuration the restart rows reopen; file-journals over\n285\t  the world's own scratch root by default); `:store` overrides the\n286\t  content store (the cut store of the D16 storage rows).  Public: the\n287\t  REPL wiring rows drive this world.\"\n288\t  [& {:keys [inbound journals store]}]\n289\t  (let [dir (temp-dir)\n290\t        jroot (temp-dir)\n291\t        journals (or journals (compose/file-journals jroot))\n292\t        backend (get (file-journal/backend! dir) ::file-journal/backend)\n293\t        clock (atom {:s 1})\n294\t        store (or store (mem/create-content-mem))\n295\t        prog (int-stream \"prog-c\")\n296\t        opened (compose/open! {:source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n297\t                               :mode :exclusive\n298\t                               :failure-model :process-crash\n299\t                               :backend backend\n300\t                               :duration {:s 30}\n301\t                               :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n302\t                               :store store\n303\t                               :diagnostics (log-writer)\n304\t                               :medium \"compose-test\"\n305\t                               :clock (fn [] @clock)\n306\t                               :journals journals})\n307\t        c (get opened ::compose/composition)\n308\t        attaches (atom 0)\n309\t        attach! (fn [descriptor]\n310\t                  (swap! attaches inc)\n311\t                  ((attach-over {\"prog-c\" prog}) descriptor))\n312\t        source-config (merge (holder-seams \"prog-c\" {})\n313\t                             {:machine (parked-reader-over (int-stream \"prog-c\"))\n314\t                              :attach! attach!\n315\t                              :inbound inbound})\n316\t        c (compose/source c \"h1\" source-config)]\n317\t    {:dir dir\n318\t     :jroot jroot\n319\t     :backend backend\n320\t     :store store\n321\t     :clock clock\n322\t     :prog prog\n323\t     :attaches attaches\n324\t     :journals journals\n325\t     :source-config source-config\n326\t     :c c\n327\t     :inbound (get-in c [:inbounds \"h1\"])}))\n328\t\n329\t\n330\t(defn reopened-world\n331\t  \"A fresh composition over the same stable configuration -- the same\n332\t  authority directory, the same journal substrate, the same store,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306c61e-3078-4fbf-aeb8-718be5db0962","uuid":"c1999fec-ebc2-4e25-9dc8-50637bc65877","timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:30:06.505Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c/test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc","content":"\n\n(defn- holder-seams\n  \"The holder's own seams over program identity `p`.\"\n  [p attach-table]\n  {:protection {p :at-least-once}\n   :receiver (s/new-machine)\n   :attach! (attach-over attach-table)\n   :observe! (observe-over)\n   :serve! (serve-as p)})\n\n\n(defn fork-world\n  \"A fork composition (the caller's selection) over one source machine.\n  No authority, no judge, no fronts: the composition's own decision.\n  Public: the no-yin.repl subprocess drives it.\"\n  []\n  (compose/open! {:source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n                  :mode :fork\n                  :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n                  :store (mem/create-content-mem)\n                  :diagnostics (log-writer)\n                  :medium \"compose-test\"\n                  :clock (fn [] {:s 1})}))\n\n\n(defn driven-fork-composition\n  \"A fork composition whose single source has run to its :lifted answer:\n  the whole drive a fresh process performs in the no-yin.repl row.\"\n  []\n  (let [c (get (fork-world) ::compose/composition)\n        c (compose/source c \"h1\"\n                          (merge (holder-seams \"prog-f\" {\"prog-f\" (int-stream \"prog-f\")})\n                                 {:machine (parked-reader-over (int-stream \"prog-f\"))}))]\n    (drive c \"h1\" (phase-of :lifted) 8)))\n\n\n(defn exclusive-world\n  \"An exclusive composition over a file-backed authority (the backend\n  that passes the gate for :process-crash) in a fresh scratch directory,\n  one source holder over a real parked machine, its journals on a\n  file-backed substrate over a scratch root of its own.  The receiver\n  attaches its own instance of the program stream, the instance the run\n  reads; `:attaches` counts its attach calls.  `:inbound` overrides the\n  composition's ring -- the bounded medium the drain rows supply;\n  `:journals` overrides the composition's journal substrate (the stable\n  recovery configuration the restart rows reopen; file-journals over\n  the world's own scratch root by default); `:store` overrides the\n  content store (the cut store of the D16 storage rows).  Public: the\n  REPL wiring rows drive this world.\"\n  [& {:keys [inbound journals store]}]\n  (let [dir (temp-dir)\n        jroot (temp-dir)\n        journals (or journals (compose/file-journals jroot))\n        backend (get (file-journal/backend! dir) ::file-journal/backend)\n        clock (atom {:s 1})\n        store (or store (mem/create-content-mem))\n        prog (int-stream \"prog-c\")\n        opened (compose/open! {:source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n                               :mode :exclusive\n                               :failure-model :process-crash\n                               :backend backend\n                               :duration {:s 30}\n                               :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n                               :store store\n                               :diagnostics (log-writer)\n                               :medium \"compose-test\"\n                               :clock (fn [] @clock)\n                               :journals journals})\n        c (get opened ::compose/composition)\n        attaches (atom 0)\n        attach! (fn [descriptor]\n                  (swap! attaches inc)\n                  ((attach-over {\"prog-c\" prog}) descriptor))\n        source-config (merge (holder-seams \"prog-c\" {})\n                             {:machine (parked-reader-over (int-stream \"prog-c\"))\n                              :attach! attach!\n                              :inbound inbound})\n        c (compose/source c \"h1\" source-config)]\n    {:dir dir\n     :jroot jroot\n     :backend backend\n     :store store\n     :clock clock\n     :prog prog\n     :attaches attaches\n     :journals journals\n     :source-config source-config\n     :c c\n     :inbound (get-in c [:inbounds \"h1\"])}))\n\n\n(defn reopened-world\n  \"A fresh composition over the same stable configuration -- the same\n  authority directory, the same journal substrate, the same store,","numLines":95,"startLine":238,"totalLines":1122}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kqv5rR2YVnX3CmZciBkwsV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
