e semantics: the root is the semantic identity of the continuation, a changed counter is a different continuation state; the plan's §1.1 row-1 line (\"id-counter variant, equal baseline\") is the stale text (F3 below).\n   - No vacuous test found: every cut asserts it fired; the new source-index test asserts `pos? calls`, the refusal status and reason, no machine, no offer; the new unfenced-report test asserts the exact refusal map and an unchanged projection; the fencing lower asserts `pos?` attaches on success and `zero?` on the fail-closed case.\n   - `fencing_rows_test`: lift under header with `@rs/source-index`; `lower-task` with `:exclusive`, `:protection`, `:grant` (evidence, binding, tenure, prefix); op-ids read from the pending row's slots at `write-slots`' indices (3/6/7, `rows.cljc:1170`), preserved through park → pack → lower → fenced retry, counter restored exactly; `markers` reads `[id kind & slots]` rows (layout at `rows.cljc:874`). Correct.\n3. **`handoff_v2_authority_test`.** Deleted: `authority-for`, the `offer!` of a version-2 fork (`:not-offerable`) and exclusive (`:committed`), and the `report!` of a halted version-2 fork. All three exercise the authority over version-2 bytes, a path that no longer exists (7a D1). Kept, renamed: the inspector's fork/exclusive baselines and the halted result's origin, on all four engines; `a-fork-tree-refuses-a-carried-operation-id` untouched. Rows-side coverage of the deleted claims exists: `grant_test` `offers-the-authority-cannot-hold-are-refused` (`:not-offerable`, `:uninspectable` for a fork pack) and `completion_test` `a-halted-body-must-name-this-occurrence-and-lease` (`:wrong-origin`), plus the new `a-composed-authority-refuses-an-unfenced-result-report-test`. Nothing that remains lost coverage; nothing deleted was about remaining code. The ns docstring misnames the covering suite (F2).\n4. **Stage E errors**: see the quick lane row; the five are the only red UCF tests and the cause is the missing `:source-index` at `open!`, 7d's.\n5. **Slow deftests**: green, see the lane table.\n6. **Portability read.** No `for`, no `#'`/private access across namespaces (everything used from `rows-support`, `rows-checkpoint-fixtures`, `rows`, `export`, `rows.checkpoint` is public), catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` in the three new try sites, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)` order kept on the subprocess test, base64 only through `jing/base64->bytes` with `(vec …)` equality (driver_test), `(comp vec reverse)` on the rows vector, `(str (random-uuid))` was already in the file. Unverified on Node/Dart by instruction.\n7. **Mutants**: table below.\n\n## Mutants (mine)\n\nDriver `target/7c-review/mut.py`; per-mutant diff, log and backup under `target/7c-review/mutants/`; each restore byte-compared and `git diff --quiet` on the file. Scoped to the named suites, quick tier.\n\n| Mutant | File | Killed? | By |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R01 recovery stored after the pack | driver | yes (8) | `the-source-half-mints-fences-and-offers-before-candidacy-test` (F1), `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` |\n| R02 custody stage after attach | rows | yes (41) | four zero-attach deftests of `rows_custody_test`, `row-2`, `row-7-a-successor-whose-lower-fails`, the fencing fail-closed case |\n| R03a grant `:not-holder` check removed | rows | yes (24) | `every-grant-check-refuses-before-any-attachment` only |\n| R03b `accept-grant!` skipped (nil state) in the compose path | rows | yes (304) | 40 deftests across compose-rows, fencing, rows-custody |\n| R04 fenced lower gates `:running` | rows | yes (1) | `an-exclusive-blocked-root-under-fenced-skips-the-grant` only (as 7b F6 predicted; export/driver mask it via `extract-recovered`) |\n| R05 offer carries the recovery address instead of the pack address | driver | yes (560) | 66 deftests across compose, compose-rows, driver |\n| R06 store ack journaled before the put | driver | yes (6) | `serving-and-storage-have-write-ahead-brackets-test`, `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` |\n| R06b test substrate: cut `:before`/`:after` meaning swapped | compose_rows_test | yes (1+1) | `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` (codex's M6 confirmed) |\n| R07a compose hands the driver an empty source index | compose | yes (337) | 47 deftests incl. `the-source-index-is-read-from-the-composition-test`, the no-REPL subprocess test |\n| R07b `open!`'s `check!` for `:source-index` removed | compose | **no** (0) | none: every composition in the suites supplies the index; no test pins the open-time refusal (F1) |\n| R08a `:wrong-origin` never | completion | yes (13) | `a-composed-authority-refuses-an-unfenced-result-report-test`, `a-halted-body-must-name-this-occurrence-and-lease`, `the-report-verifies-its-successor` |\n| R08b halted result skips the origin check | completion | yes (5) | the same first two |\n| R09a fence record not journaled | driver | yes (98) | 45 deftests |\n| R09b fence journaled without storing either object | driver | yes (28+26) | 31 deftests incl. both cut suites and `failed-recovery-store-does-not-attempt-the-body-store-test` |\n| R10 Q3 record-address conjunct → `contains?` | rows | yes (2) | `the-install-response-is-verified-before-any-attachment` (F2) |\n| R11 lift stops refusing missing trees | rows | yes (4) | `the-lift-takes-trees-from-the-composition-source-index-test`, `the-source-index-is-read-from-the-composition-test` |\n| R12 inspector drops `:yin.k/root` from the baseline | rows/checkpoint | yes (4+13) | `a-conflicting-variant-is-refused`, the content-store cuts, 13 compose-rows exit/recovery tests |\n\nCodex's nine mutants are consistent with mine where they overlap (M1↔R01, M2↔R02, M3↔R03b, M4↔R04, M5↔R05, M6↔R06b, M7↔R07a, M8↔R08a, M9↔R10). Codex's claim that all eight requested mutants are caught holds; the one survivor here is a mutant outside the brief's list.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | severity | file:line | finding | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 |