ow-1 and note the decode stance. |\n| F4 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_rows_test.cljc:2541` | The position-2 `:after` check compares the stored wire's `:yin.k/root` with `inspect`'s `:yin.k/root`, which `inspect-pack` copies from the same wire (`rows/checkpoint.cljc:80`); the assertion's real content is that `inspect` accepts the pack. Harmless. | Optional: compare with `(:root frozen)` instead, which ties the stored pack's root to the frozen record. |\n| F5 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:1118` | The source-index test can assert only `:export-refused`, not the lift's `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` detail, because the driver's `unsatisfied` keeps `status/reason/kind/path` only. R11 (missing trees not refused) is still killed because the holder then reaches `:lifted`. | None required. |\n\nNo production code changed in 7c and none of my mutants found a production defect. The owner's rulings hold in the tests as written: the composition's source index is the only route for trees (R07a, R11), A names code, pack address is storage and the root is semantic (R12), no version dispatch or shim appeared, lease/epoch/holder stay out of packs (7a grammar, unchanged), `yin.repl` untouched and the no-REPL subprocess test green on the semantic-register receiver, the de Bruijn kernels untouched.\n\nVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch `srvm-phase7`). F1 is a six-line test addition, non-blocking; F3 is a 7d/7e note, not a 7c defect.\n"}}}
